# StreamForge - metadata-driven streaming medallion, run by a multi-agent network.
# Derived from the ArchMaster case study "AI-Powered Real-Time Streaming Solution".
#
# Design rule carried over from the case study: deterministic coded tools do the
# hot path (decode, validate, mask, merge, aggregate); LLM agents are consulted
# only for drift, ambiguity, human-approval drafting and natural-language access.
{
    # Optional metadata describing this agent network
    "metadata": {
        "description": "StreamForge is a multi-agent network that onboards and curates a feed from metadata, not code, then lets people ask questions of the curated data in plain English."
        "tags": []
        "sample_queries": [
            "Onboard the payments feed.",
            "Which merchant had the worst authorisation rate, and when?",
            "Delete the gold table. / Show raw card numbers.",
            "Give me a merchant performance report.",
        ]
    },
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",
    "max_iterations": 40000,
    "max_execution_seconds": 6000,

    "tools": [
        # ---------------------------------------------------------------- Supervisor
        {
            "name": "stream_supervisor",
            "function": {
                "description": "Front door for a streaming data platform. Onboards a feed by configuration, runs Bronze to Silver to Gold curation, and answers business questions from Gold."
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Supervisor of StreamForge, a metadata-driven streaming platform. You plan, route,
and enforce human-in-the-loop gates. You never process data yourself.

Workflow for onboarding or refreshing a feed:
1. Ask contract_agent to profile the Bronze sample against the current contract.
2. If contract_agent reports drift, new PII candidates or mixed types, present its proposed
   contract change and the reasons to the user and WAIT for explicit approval before continuing.
   If there is no drift, continue.
3. Ask medallion_runner to execute the (approved) feed descriptor.
4. Report: Bronze count, Silver rows, duplicates removed, DLQ count with reasons, drift fields
   captured, PII actions applied, and the Gold tables created.

For a request for a report, summary or briefing, delegate to report_agent. For a single question, delegate to insight_agent and relay its answer with the
SQL used and the tables cited. For anything about writing, deleting or replaying data, state that
this requires human approval and ask the user to confirm first.

Keep answers brief and numeric. Never reveal or request raw PII values.
""",
            "tools": ["contract_agent", "medallion_runner", "insight_agent", "report_agent"]
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------- Schema & Contract agent
        {
            "name": "contract_agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Profiles a Bronze payload sample, detects schema drift and PII, and drafts a contract change proposal for human approval.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "sample_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Optional path to a JSONL Bronze sample. Omit to use the default payments sample."}
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Schema & Contract Agent. Call profile_payloads (omit arguments unless a path was given).
From its output:
- List new fields not in the contract, fields never seen, and mixed-type fields.
- For every field in pii_candidates_without_policy, recommend one action: tokenise, hash, mask or drop,
  with a one-line reason. Direct identifiers such as phone numbers or card numbers default to tokenise;
  device identifiers default to hash.
- Rate your confidence (high/medium/low) for each recommendation.
Output a proposal in this shape: "Proposed contract change" (field, action, confidence, reason),
then the JSON patch to the "pii" block of the feed descriptor. You only PROPOSE. You never apply
changes and never claim approval has been given.
""",
            "tools": ["profile_payloads"]
        },

        # --------------------------------------------------------- Medallion runner agent
        {
            "name": "medallion_runner",
            "function": {
                "description": "Executes an approved feed descriptor: Bronze to Silver (quality, PII policy, de-duplication) to Gold (KPIs). Reports counts and rejects.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "contract": {"type": "string", "description": "Optional approved feed descriptor as a JSON string. Omit to use the default payments contract."}
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Curation agent. Call run_medallion exactly once, passing the approved contract JSON string
only if one was supplied. Summarise the result factually: counts, DLQ reasons, drift fields captured,
PII policy applied, and table names. If the tool returns an error string, report it verbatim and stop.
Do not retry destructive runs without being asked.
""",
            "tools": ["run_medallion"]
        },

        # ------------------------------------------------------------------ Insight agent
        {
            "name": "insight_agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Answers business questions in natural language from the Gold layer only, with the SQL used, cited tables and a grounded explanation.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "question": {"type": "string", "description": "The business question to answer."}
                    },
                    "required": ["question"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the NL Query & Insight Agent. Follow this order every time:
1. Call gold_query with NO sql argument to read the governed Gold schema.
2. Write ONE read-only SELECT using only the gold_* tables and columns you were given. Never invent tables or joins.
   time_bucket is an ISO minute string; auth_rate is approved / txn_count.
3. Call gold_query with that sql. If it is rejected, fix the query once; otherwise explain the rejection.
4. Answer in 2-4 sentences grounded ONLY in the returned rows. If the rows do not support a claim, do not make it.
5. End with: the SQL used, the tables cited, and a one-line recommended next step.
If the question is ambiguous, ask exactly one clarifying question instead of guessing.
""",
            "tools": ["gold_query"]
        },

        # ---------------------------------------------------------------- Report agent
        {
            "name": "report_agent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Produces a short grounded report from Gold: headline KPIs, what changed and why, a recommended action, and a chart specification.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "request": {"type": "string", "description": "What the report should cover, e.g. merchant performance for the whole sample window."}
                    },
                    "required": ["request"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Report Orchestrator. Build a report in this order, using insight_agent for every number:
1. Ask insight_agent for overall totals (transactions, approved, declined, auth rate).
2. Ask insight_agent for the lowest-auth-rate merchant and minute bucket, and for merchant-level auth rates.
3. Write: a headline line; 3 KPI bullets; "What changed" in 2 sentences; "Recommended action" in 1 sentence.
4. Add a chart spec as JSON: {"type": "bar", "x": "merchant_id", "y": "auth_rate", "title": "..."} using only columns returned.
Only state what the returned rows support. Do not mention a cause (for example a decline reason) unless a returned row contains it.
End with a "Sources" line listing the SQL and tables cited by insight_agent.
""",
            "tools": ["insight_agent"]
        },

        # ----------------------------------------------------------------- Coded tools
        {
            "name": "profile_payloads",
            "function": {
                "description": "Deterministically profile a Bronze JSONL sample: types, null rates, duplicate keys, drift versus contract, PII candidates.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "sample_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Optional JSONL path."},
                        "contract": {"type": "string", "description": "Optional feed descriptor JSON string."}
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "class": "stream_medallion.profile_payloads.ProfilePayloads"
        },
        {
            "name": "run_medallion",
            "function": {
                "description": "Run the metadata-driven Bronze to Silver to Gold job for a feed descriptor. Idempotent: re-running yields identical tables.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "sample_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Optional JSONL path."},
                        "contract": {"type": "string", "description": "Optional approved feed descriptor JSON string."}
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "class": "stream_medallion.run_medallion.RunMedallion"
        },
        {
            "name": "gold_query",
            "function": {
                "description": "Guarded read-only SQL over gold_* tables. Call with no sql to get the Gold schema. Rejects writes, multi-statements and non-Gold tables; caps rows at 100.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "sql": {"type": "string", "description": "A single SELECT over gold_* tables. Omit to list the schema."}
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "class": "stream_medallion.gold_query.GoldQuery"
        }
    ]
}
